{
  "type": "doc",
  "content": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "text": "上ち気（(っ)わーちち）[Weather]",
          "type": "text",
          "marks": [
            {
              "type": "bold"
            },
            {
              "type": "underline"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "A friendly reminder that the Okinawan even in the titles are at this level according to the guidelines of the easiest exam.",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "Anyways, back to topic. When you want to refer to \"good weather\", you say \"いぃー\" = good and put that in front of 上ち気（(っ)わーちち）, you get: いぃー上ち気, which means \"good weather\". It is used in times like \"The weather is nice today.\" etc.",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "Furthermore, here are some words you should know in a weather report.",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "太陽（てぃーら or てぃーだ）= sun",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "晴（は）り or 晴（はり）= sunny",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": " [雲（くむ）= cloud] + [い = y] = [曇 or 雲] （くむ）い",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": " 雨 (あみ) = rain / rainy",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "雪（ゆち）= snow / snowy",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "風（かじ）= wind / windy",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "天（てぃん）= sky",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "ねー = earthquake",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "雷（かんない）= lightning",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "The reason why the last three don't need that extra い is because it already ends in an い sound.",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "暑（あち）さん = hot",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "冷（ひ or ふぃ）ーさん = cold",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "These adjectives only apply in context of weather.",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "To describe the feeling of an object (in terms of hot/cold), you use:",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "熱（あち）さん = hot",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        },
        {
          "text": "冷（ひ or ふぃ）じゅるさん = cold",
          "type": "text"
        },
        {
          "type": "hardBreak"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph"
    }
  ]
}
